        </li>
      </ul>

      <details>
        <summary><strong>Stack</strong></summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Ruby on Rails · PostgreSQL · Elasticsearch</li>
          <li>JavaScript · HTML5 · SCSS</li>
          <li>Docker · nginx · Puppet · RabbitMQ</li>
          <li>CI/CD · Capistrano · git</li>
          <li>Selenium/Capybara · Monitoring · SEO</li>
          <li>Scrivito CMS · PayPal · DocuSign · Scrum</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </article>

    <div>
      <h3>Rails Developer</h3>
      <div>
        2015-05
        <span>–</span>
        2015-11
      </div>
      <div>Berlin</div>

      <div>
        <ul>
          <li>Developed a farm management MVP.</li>
          <li>Specified/implemented REST API endpoints for mobile apps.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p>
        <b>Stack:</b>
        <small>
          <span>Ruby/Rails</span>,
          <span>PostgreSQL/PostGIS</span>,
          <span>RSpec</span>,
          <span>CI / CD</span>,
          <span>REST API</span>,
          <span>Heroku</span>,
          <span>Scrum</span>
        </small>
      </p>
    </div>

    <article aria-labelledby="developer">
      <header>
        <h3 id="developer">Developer</h3>
        <p>
          <time datetime="2011-09">Sep 2011</time>
          <span aria-hidden="true">–</span>
          <time datetime="2015-01">Jan 2015</time>
          · Oldenburg
        </p>
        <p>
          Full-stack developer at a digital agency, delivering web platforms for energy and sports clients.
        </p>
      </header>

      <ul>
        <li>Built backend system and API for a major customer’s web and mobile apps.</li>
        <li>
          Developed data-visualization portals: B2B smart-meter dashboards for retailers, and solar-plant
          monitoring tools across Europe.
        </li>
        <li>
          Delivered a new sports portal for the German Handball Bundesliga, incl. video processing,
          subscription handling, and payment integration.
        </li>
        <li>
          Introduced task runners, CI, and git workflows — laying the foundation for modernized developer
          practices at the agency.
        </li>
        <li class="hide-print">
          Forwarded use cases to sales/distribution, linking technical possibilities to business development.
        </li>
        <li class="hide-print">Shipped static websites; maintained WordPress and Joomla instances.</li>
        <li class="hide-print">Relocated to Berlin to leave comfort zone and grow professionally.</li>
      </ul>

      <details>
        <summary><strong>Stack</strong></summary>
        <ul>
          <li>HTML5 · JavaScript · SCSS · jQuery · AngularJS 1.x</li>
          <li>PHP5 · MySQL · Java · Spring · Hibernate ORM · OSGi</li>
          <li>Objective-C · WebSockets</li>
          <li>git · Subversion</li>
          <li>CI/CD · Task runners</li>
          <li>nginx · Scrum</li>
          <li>WordPress · Joomla</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </article>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="service">
    <h2 id="service">Service</h2>

    <article aria-labelledby="military">
      <h3 id="military">Military Service — IT & Network Support, German Air Force</h3>
      <p>
        <time datetime="2007-07">Jul 2007</time>
        <span aria-hidden="true">–</span>
        <time datetime="2009-02">Feb 2009</time>
        · Luftwaffe, NATO Department 6 (Orga Division)
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Provided first-line IT support and asset management at division level, supporting high-ranking
          officers and NATO staff.
        </li>
        <li>
          Maintained Windows servers, Cisco switches, and rugged client devices; connected T9 lines at
          multinational NATO exercise to link German HQ into joint networks.
        </li>
        <li>
          Developed an automated infrastructure/asset-management login tool, reducing manual effort and
          improving accuracy.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="skills">
    <h2 id="skills">Skills</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>Open skills matrix</summary>
      <SkillsMatrix categories={skills} />
    </details>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section class="case-study" aria-labelledby="cs-portal">
    <h2 id="cs-portal">
      <span aria-hidden="true">📊</span> Case study — Portal relaunch
    </h2>

    <p>
      <strong>Context:</strong> Agency-owned city portal built around interactive virtual tours with three audiences:
      municipalities, local businesses, and consumers. The product needed modernization to stay competitive and
      win longer-term B2B contracts.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>What I did:</strong> Led the relaunch end-to-end as the sole engineer: rebuilt core features while
      keeping legacy online; embedded SEO into feature design; introduced geospatial search (distance around POIs);
      created monitoring dashboards; and guided a CRM migration (data rescue/transform, customized flows, staff
      training).
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Outcomes:</strong> POI pages reached Google SERP #1 (often outranking official sites), improving
      discoverability and strengthening the sales story—especially for small businesses without a web presence.
      Operational dashboards increased visibility for management, and the renewed product secured multi-year B2B
      contracts (4+ years), creating predictable revenue and financial stability.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Notable details:</strong> SVG floorplan linter improved tour reliability (no dead links; hotspot
        reachability).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Role:</strong> concept → delivery → monitoring; client-facing demos; mentoring a working student.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="education">
    <h2 id="education">Education</h2>

    <article aria-labelledby="edu1">
      <h3 id="edu1">B.Sc. Wirtschaftsinformatik (Information Systems)</h3>
      <p>
        <time datetime="2009-03">Mar 2009</time>
        <span aria-hidden="true">–</span>
        <time datetime="2012-03">Mar 2012</time>
        · Jade University of Applied Sciences, Wilhelmshaven
      </p>
      <p>
        Thesis: <q>Software Modularity in Smart Homes – OSGi as a Base for Future Products and Services</q>
      </p>
      <p>Completed Cisco CCNA Exploration 1–4 (Network Administration).</p>
    </article>

    <article aria-labelledby="edu2">
      <h3 id="edu2">Student Assistant</h3>
      <p>
        <time datetime="2009">2009</time>
        <span aria-hidden="true">–</span>
        <time datetime="2011">2011</time>
        · Jade University of Applied Sciences, Wilhelmshaven
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Tutor for programming course (Winter 2009).</li>
        <li>Research assistant on <q>Mobile Smart Metering</q> project (Summer 2011).</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <aside>
    <p>
      Are you looking for code examples? Head over to
      <a href="/projects">my projects</a>
      or <a href="https://github.com/gildesmarais/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">my Github profile</a>.
    </p>
  </aside>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Always-visible, readable link underlines (dark & light) */
  :where(main a) {
    text-decoration-line: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 0.08em;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
    text-decoration-skip-ink: auto;
  }

  /* Focus visibility without JS */
  :where(a, button, summary, [tabindex]):focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--pico-primary);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* Make <summary> clearly interactive */
  :where(details > summary) {
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Improve skip-link usability when targeted */
  :where(:target) {
    scroll-margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  /* Prefer higher contrast when user asks for it */
  @media (prefers-contrast: more) {
    :where(main a) {
      text-decoration-thickness: 0.12em;
      text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    }
    :where(a, button, summary, [tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline-width: 3px;
    }
  }

  /* Subtle highlight without breaking Pico’s look */
  .case-study {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--pico-primary);
    padding: 1rem 1rem 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pico-background-color) 92%, var(--pico-primary) 8%);
  }

  /* Keep headings tight inside the box */
  .case-study h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
